<figure class="core-figure">
 <div class="drawing" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Index references and a heap page; scroll horizontally on a narrow screen">
 <svg viewBox="0 0 680 365" role="img" aria-labelledby="core-read-title core-read-desc">
  <title id="core-read-title">An index finds a location; a heap page supplies the version</title>
  <desc id="core-read-desc">A branching index page chooses the leaf containing key 7. That leaf associates 7 with heap location page zero, item seven. Item seven points to tuple bytes containing product 7 and available 3. The snapshot still decides whether those bytes describe a visible version.</desc>
  <defs><marker id="core-read-arrow" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" refX="6" refY="3.5" orient="auto"><path d="M0 0L7 3.5L0 7Z" class="arrowhead" /></marker></defs>
  <text x="20" y="25" class="heading">The executor asks for product_id = 7</text>
  <rect x="20" y="47" width="640" height="290" rx="5" class="boundary" />
  <text x="34" y="72" class="minor">Index and heap pages accessed through shared buffers</text>
  <rect x="38" y="95" width="206" height="53" class="page" />
  <text x="51" y="115">Branching index page</text><text x="51" y="136" class="mono">below 5001 → left child</text>
  <path d="M140 150V181" class="pointer" />
  <rect x="38" y="188" width="206" height="119" class="page" />
  <text x="51" y="210">Ordered leaf entries</text>
  <text x="51" y="237" class="mono">6 → (0,6)</text>
  <rect x="45" y="246" width="190" height="27" class="selected" />
  <text x="51" y="265" class="mono">7 → (0,7)</text>
  <text x="51" y="293" class="mono">8 → (0,8)</text>
  <path d="M245 260H289V141H326" class="pointer" />
  <rect x="333" y="95" width="308" height="212" class="page" />
  <text x="347" y="117">Heap page 0</text>
  <rect x="347" y="130" width="281" height="28" class="selected" />
  <text x="356" y="149" class="mono">item 7 → tuple byte offset</text>
  <path d="M482 160V195" class="pointer" />
  <rect x="347" y="203" width="281" height="86" class="tuple" />
  <text x="359" y="225" class="mono">product_id 7 · available 3</text>
  <text x="359" y="250">creator / updater information</text>
  <text x="359" y="273" class="minor">Check against this query’s snapshot</text>
  <text x="20" y="357" class="minor">Schematic index keys. The tuple location (0,7) was observed in the lab.</text>
 </svg>
 </div>
 <figcaption>The index entry names a heap page and an item on that page. The item points to the tuple’s bytes, so moving bytes within the page need not move the item number. Finding that version and deciding whether to return it are separate operations.</figcaption>
</figure>
